benchmark: zengif find_nearest branchless chunked-min optimization (ARM A/B)
date: 2026-05-29
hostname: Hetzner cax21 (arm-zen-ubuntu), ARM Neoverse-N1 aarch64, 4 cores, 7.5 GB RAM
toolchain: cargo 1.96.0 (30a34c682 2026-05-25)
rustflags: '' (runtime SIMD dispatch; NO target-cpu=native, per benchmarking discipline)
build: cargo build --release -j2 --bench codec
bench_cmd: target/release/deps/codec-* --bench   (zenbench criterion-compat, all groups)
local_commit_under_test: fd5c2b86ace1 (sibling workspace zengif--arm-perf; lands on main)
parent_main_commit: a6b11773 (ci: build fuzz targets for host gnu target)

method:
  Single source tree, src/types.rs swapped between two versions and rebuilt:
    BASELINE  src/types.rs: scalar `if dist < best_dist` scan
              (marker check on box: chunks_exact=0 best_dist=3)
    OPTIMIZED src/types.rs: branchless chunked (dist<<8)|index running-min
              (marker check on box: chunks_exact=1 best_dist=1)
  Both phases verified to recompile (18.2s / 18.34s; not a cached-binary skip).
  Optimized file integrity verified by md5 match local<->box:
    68f52c4372126e5aeb2e2102c33a139c

result_summary:
  find_nearest-bound encode path: 1.10x - 1.13x faster (-8.8% to -11.3% wall time).
  decode path (control, no find_nearest): unchanged within noise (<=0.5%).

correctness:
  Byte-identical encoded GIF output, baseline vs optimized, across all corpus files
  (benchmarks/zengif_find_nearest_correctness_2026-05-29.tsv). cargo test = 162 passed,
  0 failed. The (dist<<8)|index packing preserves lowest-index tie-break; the
  transparent-pixel short-circuit and dist==0 early-exit are retained.

raw_log: zen-arm-results/zengif/zengif_arm_bench3.log (off-repo; full zenbench output)
x86_local_microbench (7950X, isolated find_nearest loop, runtime dispatch):
  grad+full256 1.121x | few+exact 1.172x | grad+exact256 1.166x | 0 mismatches
